                <head>293. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>The Conference on Antarctica met at Washington, October 15–December 1, with
                    representatives of Argentina, Australia, Belgium, Chile, France, Japan, New
                    Zealand, Norway, the Soviet Union, the Union of South Africa, the United
                    Kingdom, and the United States in attendance. Ambassador Herman Phleger, head of
                    the U.S. Delegation, was elected chairman of the conference. The first plenary
                    session was held October 15 from 11 a.m. to 12:30 p.m. and from 3 to 4:30 p.m.
                    in the auditorium of the Department of the Interior. For texts of the opening
                    statements made by each delegation, see <hi rendition="#italic">The Conference
                        on Antarctica, Washington, October 15–December 1, 1959</hi> (Washington,
                    September 1960), pages 2–30.</p>
            </div>
